        },
        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*Something pale crouches on a rock at the water's edge, all bones and long fingers, with two great pale eyes like small moons.* What is it, precious? Is it soft? Is it juicy? Sss... no, no. It's a big one, a bold one, come down into our dark with its little light. *It creeps closer, whispering.* Does it know the old game, precious? Riddles! Seven riddles we asks it, and seven answers it gives us. Guess five of the seven rightly and it wins a present from our hoard, yes, a true present. Guess fewer... and it wins nothing at all, gollum, nothing but the dark. But only once while the week lasts -- the riddles must ripen, precious, they must ripen. Does it play? Does it, precious?"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "__struct_id": 1,
        "Animation": {
